+// detector) can see them. A host whose builtin-module loader answers a value
+// that is not constructible (a scriptc-built binary, for example) must not
+// have it constructed: the fiber works without the capture. The probe runs
+// once, at module load, so the hot path never throws.
+const asyncContextSupported = /*#__PURE__*/(() => {
+  if (AsyncResource === undefined) return false;
